# Analyze the step09 sweep: report transmission, IL and splitting balance at the
# lowest-loss length.
#
# This is a single-wavelength pick, and the sweep's minimum is broad and not smooth at
# the 0.1 dB level, so the lowest point sits inside the solver's own scatter. Confirm the
# choice over the band before treating it as final.

# before running check the working directory: File -> Change working directory

############# Results #################
min_IL       = min(IL_vs_L);
idx_opt       = find(IL_vs_L, min_IL);
L_opt_IL     = L_sweep_vec(idx_opt);

L_opt        = L_opt_IL;
T_top_opt    = T_top_vs_L(idx_opt);
T_bot_opt    = T_bot_vs_L(idx_opt);

# imbalance at the optimum (dB); 0 = perfect 50:50
Imb_opt = abs(10 * log10(T_top_opt / T_bot_opt));

?"";
?"==============================================";
?"  MMI Length Sweep Results";
?"==============================================";
?"  Analytical L_MMI      : " + num2str(L_MMI/um,    "%.2f") + " um";
?"  Best L (min IL)        : " + num2str(L_opt_IL/um,  "%.2f") + " um";
?"";
?"  At min-loss length:";
?"    T_top  = " + num2str(T_top_opt, "%.4f") + "  (" + num2str(10*log10(T_top_opt), "%.2f") + " dB)";
?"    T_bot  = " + num2str(T_bot_opt, "%.4f") + "  (" + num2str(10*log10(T_bot_opt), "%.2f") + " dB)";
?"    IL     = " + num2str(min_IL,    "%.3f") + " dB";
?"    Imb    = " + num2str(Imb_opt,   "%.3f") + " dB";
?"==============================================";
?"";
##########################################
